comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T07:42:22.476Z",codex-agent,"Baseline npm ls braces fast-glob micromatch shows fast-glob 3.3.3 -> micromatch 4.0.8 -> braces 3.0.3, also the optional peer of pm-ops 2026.10.6. Production-only tree is empty. The production duplication launcher and raw coverage inventory already use node:fs globSync; fast-glob has no direct code import. Refresh pm-ops to latest published 2026.10.14 and remove the direct peer. CI already has workflow_dispatch; use the prescribed pm-github 2026.10.14 fallback pending release and repin. No sync execution or repository settings changes."
  "2026-10-15T07:49:21.519Z",codex-agent,"Related work: pm-vcs-qfku tracks the removed vulnerable dependency chain; pm-vcs-1bcq records the reproduced Node 22 GC measurement race and one-flag deterministic test fix with flag-only revert and held-corpus negative controls. The fallback reusable workflow predates caller-changelog regeneration and CI dispatch from pm-github PR 122; the later 2026.10.15 repin remains an operational dependency."
  "2026-10-15T07:49:51.061Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked validation passes: npm run typecheck; npm run duplicates (65 sources, 0 clone pairs); retained-corpus focused test 1/1. The one-flag measurement fix has a flag-removal failing revert and a genuinely retained corpus failing control. Preparing the committed self-host snapshot before full isolated npm and Bun release gates. Both workflow/dependency changes preserve runtime code and quality thresholds."
